  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Northern Kenya Marsabit Drought response 2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The current drought in Marsabit Northern Kenya is as a result of rain failure of the last two rainy seasons and failure of short rains-October- December 2016 (in some sections) which has culminated into disruption of social/economic livelihood of vulnerable population in Marsabit County.  Most the households are facing food security challenges, water scarcity and loss of their prime Livelihood (livestock) among others. A Joint interagency rapid assessment led by National Drought Management Authority (NDMA) has been carried out and their report has confirmed the severity of the situation.  Additionaly Caritas Marsabit has explored particular locations; Chimbe and Yaa Othola areas, to confirm the magnitude  of drought situation. Both reports confirms the deteriorating situation and the need for assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
